{
  "slug": "accessibility-writing",
  "concept": "Accessibility Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "Reference for writing content that is usable by screen-reader users, low-vision users, deaf and hard-of-hearing users, users with cognitive disabilities, and users on assistive tech.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Accessibility Writing",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Reference for writing content that is usable by screen-reader users, low-vision users, deaf and hard-of-hearing users, users with cognitive disabilities, and users on assistive tech.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#accessibility-writing",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The 8-point accessibility-writing test",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Headings form a proper outline. Exactly one <h1> per page. No skipped levels.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#the-8-point-accessibility-writing-test",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Every image has an alt attribute. Decorative images use alt=\"\". Informative images get a 1–2 sentence description.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#the-8-point-accessibility-writing-test",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Every link reads as a self-contained label. \"Click here,\" \"read more,\" \"learn more,\" and bare URLs fail.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#the-8-point-accessibility-writing-test",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Every form control has a programmatically associated label. <label for> matched to input id.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#the-8-point-accessibility-writing-test",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Every icon-only button has an accessible name. aria-label describing the action (\"Close dialog,\" not \"X icon\").",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#the-8-point-accessibility-writing-test",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Information is never conveyed by color alone. Status indicated by \"Error: …\" prefix or icon plus color.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#the-8-point-accessibility-writing-test",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The page declares its language. <html lang=\"en\">.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#the-8-point-accessibility-writing-test",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Time-based media has alternatives. Video has synchronized captions and a transcript.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#the-8-point-accessibility-writing-test",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. Alt text by image purpose",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Decorative images - alt=\"\" (empty, not missing).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#1-alt-text-by-image-purpose",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Informative images - describe the information the image carries: alt=\"CPU usage spikes to 95% at 14:30 UTC then returns to baseline by 14:35.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#1-alt-text-by-image-purpose",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Functional images - describe the action or destination: alt=\"View cart\" (NOT alt=\"shopping cart icon\")",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#1-alt-text-by-image-purpose",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Complex images - short alt plus a long description: alt=\"Latency percentile chart for production over the past 24 hours.\" Plus aria-describedby pointing to a <figcaption> with full details.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#1-alt-text-by-image-purpose",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Heading structure",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "One <h1> per page. The page title.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#2-heading-structure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "No skipped levels going down. After <h2> you may use another <h2> or an <h3>. You may not jump to <h5>.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#2-heading-structure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Headings are not for styling. Don't use <h3> because it looks right.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#2-heading-structure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Descriptive headings. \"Introduction\" fails WCAG 2.4.6. \"How to reset your password\" passes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#2-heading-structure",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Link text",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Don't include the word \"link\" in link text. Screen readers already announce that an element is a link.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#3-link-text",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "For downloadable files, include the file format: Download the Q1 incident report (PDF, 1.2 MB).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#3-link-text",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Form labels",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "<label for> matched to input id. The most robust.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#4-form-labels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Wrapped <label>. Works without explicit for/id.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#4-form-labels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "aria-labelledby pointing at a visible element.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#4-form-labels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "aria-label. Last resort only when no visible label is possible.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#4-form-labels",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Icon-only buttons",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The aria-label describes what the button does (\"Close dialog,\" \"Search,\" \"Open menu\"). NOT what it looks like (\"X,\" \"Magnifying glass\").",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#5-icon-only-buttons",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Color independence (WCAG 1.4.1)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Status with a prefix word. \"Error: Email is invalid.\" \"Warning: Unsaved changes.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#6-color-independence-wcag-141",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Status with an icon plus color. A red X icon plus the word \"Failed.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#6-color-independence-wcag-141",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Links underlined as well as colored.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#6-color-independence-wcag-141",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Captions, transcripts, audio descriptions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "1.2.2 Captions (prerecorded), Level A. Synchronized captions for prerecorded video with audio.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#7-captions-transcripts-audio-descriptions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "1.2.4 Captions (live), Level AA. Live captions for live audio.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#7-captions-transcripts-audio-descriptions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "1.2.5 Audio description (prerecorded), Level AA. Audio description of prerecorded video.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#7-captions-transcripts-audio-descriptions",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. The \"skip to main content\" link",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The skip link is the first focusable element on the page.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#9-the-skip-to-main-content-link",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "It is visually hidden until focused.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/accessibility-writing/#9-the-skip-to-main-content-link",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
